  "body": {
    "id": "prop:honest-length-loose-bracket",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For every \\(d\\le c_\\epsilon n\\log(en)\\), the currently established\nsame-class confidence-length bounds are\n\\[\n r_{n,d,M}\\lesssim_{\\epsilon,\\alpha}\n \\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\\le4M.\n\\]\nThe upper inequality is attained by the deterministic interval\n\\([-2M,2M]\\); no direct calibration or Gaussian approximation is used.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(d\\)",
      "\\(c_{\\epsilon}\\)",
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(\\epsilon\\)",
      "\\(M\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)",
      "\\(r_{n,d,M}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:cell-mean-envelope",
      "def:global-law-class",
      "def:ate-functional",
      "def:minimax-honest-length",
      "def:frontier-scale",
      "thm:same-class-testing-converse"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "The lower inequality is exactly\n\\(thm:same\\text{-}class\\text{-}testing\\text{-}converse\\), whose range\ncondition is the displayed restriction on \\(d\\).  For the upper inequality,\n\\(ass:cell\\text{-}mean\\text{-}envelope\\) and\n\\(def:ate\\text{-}functional\\) imply\n\\[\n |\\tau(P)|\n \\le\\sum_{k=1}^dp_k\\{|\\mu_{1k}|+|\\mu_{0k}|\\}\n \\le2M\n\\]\nfor every \\(P\\in\\mathcal P_{d,\\epsilon,M}\\).  Therefore the deterministic\ninterval \\(C_n^0=[-2M,2M]\\) has coverage one under every\n\\(Q_P^{(n)}\\), is admissible in the infimum of\n\\(def:minimax\\text{-}honest\\text{-}length\\), and has length \\(4M\\).\nTaking the required supremum and infimum proves\n\\(\\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\\le4M\\).",
    "justification": "This records the strongest closed two-sided confidence-length statement presently justified by the core.",
    "gap": "The upper endpoint \\(4M\\) is the deterministic range interval, so matching it to the lower scale remains the global calibration problem.",
    "consumer": "It gives an honest fallback benchmark while the sharp constructive upper bound is unresolved.",
